# Class-ref-typed statics across packages. The producer types a static's global
# and function signature after its class struct types are recorded, so it names
# `(ref $Zed)`; the consumer must too. Reconstruction visits classes
# parents-first then alphabetically, so were statics imported during it,
# `Alpha`'s would be declared while `Zed` — neither its ancestor nor
# alphabetically before it — still had no recorded struct type. Hence the
# separate pass. `static_ref_types_cross_package` covers only types whose
# lowering doesn't depend on that ordering.
# name          dir    deps          root
@test/zlib      lib    -
main            app    @test/zlib    root
